course: dictionary
lesson: 2403
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «The drink tastes of cherry-tart, custard, pine-apple, roast turkey, toffee and hot buttered toast.» Custard is in a list of tasty things, so it is a food, not a tool or a place.
explain: Ask: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense. A sweet yellow sauce fits: the drink tastes of a sweet yellow sauce. That works, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Different places use the same word differently. In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, custard is usually the sweet yellow sauce poured over puddings. In the US, custard can mean frozen custard, a kind of ice cream. The clues around the word, and where the text is set, tell you which one is meant.
fact: Custard is a noun. It can mean the sauce, as in «some custard», or a dessert, as in «a custard».
fact: Custard is a sweet yellow sauce made from milk, eggs or custard powder and sugar, poured over puddings.
fact: A custard can also be a soft, set dessert of milk and eggs, often baked, like an egg custard or a custard tart.
fact: In the US, custard can mean frozen custard, a kind of ice cream.
fact: Custard thickens when it is heated: the egg proteins set, and cornflour makes it swell.
exercise: «The drink tastes of cherry-tart, custard, pine-apple, roast turkey, toffee and hot buttered toast.» In this list, what kind of thing is custard? | A place to visit | A type of shoe | *A sweet food | A kind of animal
exercise: According to the dictionary, what is custard made from? | Oil, vinegar and tomatoes | Water, ice and lemons | *Milk, eggs or custard powder, and sugar | Flour, butter and salt
exercise: In the US, custard can mean frozen custard. What is that? | A cold, fizzy drink | *A kind of ice cream | A dry biscuit | A bowl of hot soup
test: «Lila poured warm custard over her apple crumble.» What does custard mean here? | *A sweet yellow sauce | A cold drink | A small cake | A kind of bread
test: Ben says custard turns thick when it is heated. Why does this happen? | The sugar melts away into the air | *The egg proteins set and the cornflour swells | The custard turns into bread | The custard freezes into ice
exam: Which is the best way to check the meaning of a word in a sentence? | Ask someone to read it aloud | Look only at the first letter of the word | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Skip the sentence and guess
